{"title": "Google Pixel held its ground in the US despite a middling Pixel 11 launch", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/20/google-pixel-us-smartphone-market-q3-2026/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/08/pixel-11-pro-xl-canyon-9.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The latest quarterly data for the US smartphone market reveals that Google Pixel is holding its ground despite the overall market faltering, and the other two major Android brands struggling.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/20/google-pixel-us-smartphone-market-q3-2026/#more-739291\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-20T08:30:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-22T17:44:42.485929+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
